---
import LabsLayout from "../../layouts/labs.astro";
---

<LabsLayout title="Scenario E — Artifact SQL (DuckDB) — Querial Labs" active="e">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Scenario E</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Artifact SQL (DuckDB)</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                This is the lab that shows how <code class="text-foreground">artifact-sql</code>
                works. DuckDB runs <strong class="text-foreground">inside an eligible agent</strong>
                — no extra warehouse, no connection on the transform step. You will run
                single-input CAST/filter steps, then a <strong class="text-foreground">two-input JOIN + GROUP BY</strong>
                that writes <code class="text-foreground">aw.sales_order_summary</code> on both destinations.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/downloads/scenario-e-artifacts.zip" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-querial-indigo px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:opacity-90">
                Download scenario-e-artifacts.zip
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/run-through" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Load and test
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/devops-artifacts" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Artifacts docs
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Handler contracts
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/developer-join-mode" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Wait all / Wait any
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>What Artifact SQL is for</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Read one or more Parquet artifacts from earlier steps in the <strong class="text-foreground">same run</strong>.</li>
                <li>Author ordinary SQL. DuckDB registers one inbound file as <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input }}"}</code>, or several as <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input.outputName }}"}</code>.</li>
                <li>Write a new Parquet (<code class="text-foreground">config.outputName</code>). Downstream staged sinks consume that file.</li>
                <li>No logical connection, no schema source, no secrets. <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code> must point at a Succeeded producer.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Package</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package <code class="text-foreground">aw-scenario-e</code>, pipeline <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_e</code>, revision <code class="text-foreground">duckdb-join-v1</code>.</li>
                <li>Stubs: <code class="text-foreground">aw-source</code>, <code class="text-foreground">aw-sql-dest</code>, <code class="text-foreground">aw-pg-dest</code>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Topology</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>extract_sales_order (ROOT, parquet)
  ├─ transform_sales_order (artifact-sql, one input: CAST/filter)
  │     ├─ load_sales_order_sqlserver / load_sales_order_postgres
  │     └─ transform_order_summary (artifact-sql, TWO inputs: JOIN + GROUP BY)
  │           ├─ load_order_summary_sqlserver
  │           └─ load_order_summary_postgres
  └─ extract_sales_line (succeeded)
        └─ transform_sales_line (artifact-sql, one input)
              ├─ load_sales_line_* (also waits on matching order load)
              └─ transform_order_summary (second input)</code></pre>
            <p>
                One structural root. All transform/sink edges are
                <code class="text-foreground">artifact_available</code>.
            </p>

            <h2>DuckDB steps in this package</h2>
            <h3 class="text-foreground text-lg font-semibold">1. Single-input CAST</h3>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">transform_sales_order</code> /
                <code class="text-foreground">transform_sales_line</code> each have one
                list <code class="text-foreground">inputs</code> row. SQL uses
                <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input }}"}</code> plus
                <code class="text-foreground">CAST(...)</code> and a filter so the join
                consumes typed Parquet, not the raw extract.
            </p>
            <h3 class="text-foreground text-lg font-semibold">2. Multi-input JOIN + aggregate</h3>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">transform_order_summary</code> is the teaching step:
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>config:
  outputName: order_summary
  inputs:
    - from_step: transform_sales_order
    - from_step: transform_sales_line</code></pre>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>SELECT
    o.sales_order_id,
    o.customer_id,
    CAST(o.order_date AS DATE) AS order_day,
    COUNT(*) AS line_count,
    SUM(l.order_qty) AS total_qty,
    SUM(l.line_total) AS computed_line_total,
    o.total_due AS header_total_due
FROM {"{{ input.sales_order_transformed }}"} AS o
INNER JOIN {"{{ input.sales_line_transformed }}"} AS l
    ON o.sales_order_id = l.sales_order_id
GROUP BY
    o.sales_order_id,
    o.customer_id,
    CAST(o.order_date AS DATE),
    o.total_due;</code></pre>
            <p>
                Qualifiers are the producer <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code>
                values, frozen when the edge is saved — not YAML map keys. Single-input
                CAST steps use the bare token <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input }}"}</code>.
                Staged loads bind <code class="text-foreground">from_step: transform_order_summary</code>
                as a list row and upsert <code class="text-foreground">aw.sales_order_summary</code>.
                <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="text-link hover:underline">Handler contracts</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Migrations (E-only summary table)</h2>
            <p>
                Shared sales tables plus
                <code class="text-foreground">ss_006_create_sales_summary</code> /
                <code class="text-foreground">pg_006_create_sales_summary</code>
                after <code class="text-foreground">005</code>. Use deployment
                <code class="text-foreground">before_run</code> on first pass.
            </p>

            <h2>Flags (required)</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:Artifacts=true</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:DuckDb=true</code></li>
            </ul>
            <p>Every transform and every sink in E needs both. Agents must advertise DuckDB.</p>

            <h2>Walkthrough extras</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li>Import the zip. Resolve all three connections.</li>
                <li>Designer: three DuckDB nodes (no connection badge on them). <code class="text-foreground">transform_order_summary</code> has two inbound artifact edges and stays Wait all — Wait any is rejected on Artifact SQL. See <a href="/docs/developer-join-mode" class="text-link hover:underline">Wait all and Wait any</a>.</li>
                <li>Publish: one root — no multi-root warning.</li>
                <li>Run Graph: extract → CAST transforms → join step → six sinks (order, line, summary × two dests). Inspector on the join step lists two input artifacts and output <code class="text-foreground">order_summary</code>. SQL tab is the published DuckDB, not the draft.</li>
                <li>Failed-cone: fail one staged sink; retry cone; extracts and DuckDB steps should stay Succeeded / reused. Writes are default-unsafe for in-run auto-retry; cone retry of those writes is allowed. See <a href="/docs/devops-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Retry and failed-cone</a> and <a href="/docs/developer-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Step retry policies</a>.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Verify</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.sales_order;
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.sales_order_line;
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.sales_order_summary;
-- line_count should match lines for that order
SELECT TOP 20 sales_order_id, line_count, total_qty, computed_line_total, header_total_due
FROM aw.sales_order_summary
ORDER BY sales_order_id;</code></pre>
            <p>
                Run the counts on both destinations. Summary grain is one row per order that
                still had lines after the CAST filters. PostgreSQL uses
                <code class="text-foreground">LIMIT 20</code> instead of
                <code class="text-foreground">TOP 20</code>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</LabsLayout>
